Article 3 (Applicability to release of agricultural promotion areas)
The amended provisions of Article 28(3)2 shall begin to apply to applications for the release of an agricultural promotion area filed after the enforcement of this Decree.
Article 4 (Applicability to facilities subject to restriction on permission for farmland diversion)
The amended provisions of Article 44(3) shall begin to apply to applications for permission for farmland diversion filed after this Decree enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to delegation of authority for permission and consultation)
The amended provisions of subparagraph 1 of Appendix 3 shall begin to apply to applications or receipts of a request for permission for or consultation on farmland diversion filed after this Decree enters into force.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning facilities for production of agricultural and livestock products within scope of farmland)
The amended provisions of Article 2(4) shall be governed by the former provisions with respect to the site of a facility for the production of agricultural and livestock products for which permission for farmland diversion was obtained or a report on farmland diversion was accepted under the former provisions at the time this Decree enters into force.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning restrictions on acts within agricultural protection zones)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 35 of the partially amended Enforcement Decree of the Farmland Act (Presidential Decree No. 19281), the previous provisions shall apply to restrictions on acts for a person who, before January 22, 2006 (the enforcement date of that partial amendment), obtained or applied for an authorization, permission, or approval, etc., for the installation of a building, structure, or other facility, the installation of which is prohibited within an agricultural protection area under the amended provisions of Article 35 of the that partial amendment.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning restrictions on acts within agricultural promotion areas)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 34(4) and (5) or subparagraph 3 of Article 35 of the partially amended Enforcement Decree of the Farmland Act (Presidential Decree No. 16254), the previous provisions shall apply to the standards for restrictions on acts for a person who, before April 19, 1999 (the enforcement date of that partial amendment), obtained or applied for an authorization, permission, or approval, etc., for the installation of a building, structure, or other facility, the installation of which is restricted within an agricultural promotion area under the amended provisions of Article 34(4) and (5) or subparagraph 3 of Article 35 of that partial amendment.
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning reduction of or exemption from farmland conservation charges)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Appendix 2, the reduction of or exemption from farmland conservation charges for cases where permission for farmland diversion (including an authorization or permission, etc., deemed to constitute permission for farmland diversion under other Acts) was obtained or a report on farmland diversion was filed before this Decree enters into force shall be governed by the previous provisions.
Article 10 (Transitional measures concerning ordinances on operation of Farmland Management Committees)
An ordinance of a Si (including a Special City and a Metropolitan City) or Gun concerning the operation, etc., of a Farmland Management Committee under the previous Enforcement Decree of the Farmland Lease Management Act at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed an ordinance of the relevant local government under this Decree.
Article 11 Omitted.
Article 12 (Relationship to other statutes or regulations)
Where the previous Enforcement Decree of the Farmland Act or any provisions thereof are cited in other statutes or regulations at the time this Decree enters into force, this Decree or the corresponding provisions of this Decree shall be deemed to have been cited in lieu of the previous provisions, if such corresponding provisions exist in this Decree.

